{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506231-let-s-talk-about-rotes-baby","id":1506231,"title":"Let's talk about Rotes, baby...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-23T07:11:20-07:00","id":1506231,"title":"Let's talk about Rotes, baby...","content":"As I'm trying to learn more about CofD as a whole and have moved onto Mage for a time, Rotes have caught my interest. So let's talk about Rotes. What are your favorite Rotes? Were there any that were more useful to you than you expected they would be? Any that were less useful? <br /> <br /> Reading through without any experience with the game, I absolutely love Exceptional Luck. It's everything I ever wanted in an Entropy mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T10:14:37-07:00","id":1506241,"title":"","content":"<b>Overall Great:</b><br /> <br /> <i>Acceleration:</i> Grants tremendous flexibility with initiative in combat, allows you to dodge far more effectively and gives a decent bonus to movement speed. Outside of combat, it can significantly reduce the time for extended actions.<br /> <br /> <i>Control Instincts:</i> Very versatile when all Reach are available. It can be used to create camraderie by appealing to the pack/herd instinct in social situations, cause disgust, seduce or cause a visceral lashing out. In combat, it can trigger a directed fight response, cause fear, make someone flee or make them feel so overwhelmed that they surrender. It needs a over Reach to apply a long term effect on a supernatural being from sensory range, but it still pretty good.<br /> <br /> <i>Exceptional Luck:</i> Provides generally useful dice bonuses/penalties and conditions. The reflexive option allows you to mitigate damage in whatever situation (bomb goes off, ambush, falling off a building, etc) via Charmed. Lastly, the reflexive and sensory version can shut down a dangerous opponent for a turn or work as a better version of counterspell, both done by applying Knocked Down.<br /> <br /> <b>Investigation:</b><br /> <br /> <i>Co-Location:</i> Great for creating exit strategies (link the character to their Sanctum), its a great aid for infiltration by providing warps around the scene and it allows the creation of a portal network.<br /> <br /> <i>Postcognition:</i> A solid investigation spell, but requires more Reach to be great. Temporal sympathy means you need sensory range and to beat its Withstand, which the mudra helps with. The duration and precise control allow you to get a lot more functionality for the mana.<br /> <br /> <i>Serendipity:</i> You can always find a lead for yourself and others to accomplish a goal. With the extra Reach, your insights can be tailored to leverage someone's strengths, and you can do it over the phone. &quot;What do you mean look at the conductor's music sheet ? I have a bomb to defuse and I am not a damn...oh hey, this piece is weird, its a music cypher, I am a good musician....oh wow, its the deactivation code. Thanks, you cryptic luck monster&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Combat:</b><br /> <br /> <i>Decay:</i> &quot;Those were some nice guns you were all carrying, were, past tense. You know, they don't make balconies like they used to, or lights, helicopter fans, or car wheels, or load bearing pillars. I just cast this at sensory AoE centered on you. Your weapons ? Gone. Your Dedicated Tool ? Gone. Your reinforced clothes and supplies ? Gone. Imbued items ? Gone as well.&quot; It doesn't do damage, but it can be devastating all the same.<br /> <br /> <i>Kinetic Blow:</i> Sure, the bonus it provides is capped at 5, which is made easier to obtain with a mudra, but that is still adding the force of a sniper rifle to an attack, which means wound penalties are likely to occur. Knocked Down can potentially shut down their turn. Stunned can as well, with the bonus of making them waste Willpower and have to deal with -3 to all actions, otherwise they are left at half defense. When all of these effects are put together, it means opponents need to spend Wipower to even roll to avoid being Knocked Down, doing so at a minimal penalty of -3 and likely higher thanks to wounds. A close quarter combatant just needs one good hit to utterly swing the tempo in their favor. If applied to something like a grenade, it can be a devastating move. Using it on a ranged weapon without Paradox requires ritual cast for it to last a scene, but considering some of them can apply autofire and covering fire, it can have a devastating effect.<br /> <br /> <i>Shaping:</i> Create entrances where there were none, close access points entirely, use it as an intimidation tactic by tearing steel doors with your bare hands, trap opponents in the walls or ceiling, generate instant cover, control the terrain to your liking, levitate an entire house into the air and then drop the spell so gravity finishes them off, make people faint by keeping the bare minimum of air around them, make them hallucinate by decreasing nitrogen concentration and increasing oxygen, create a dense fog by using the lake's water, use it on a sewer grate or on your jumpsuit or power suit to fly, put out a fire by removing all oxygen. Its a spell with so many creative applications, its just plain good.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-23-2023, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T10:40:28-07:00","id":1506244,"title":"","content":"As someone who has only done GMing, I really enjoyed <i>Psychic Reprogramming</i>, particularly as used by a mage on themselves. Made for interesting NPCs where the players were really interacting with a kind of facsimile personality that the mage had strategically constructed for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T11:23:54-07:00","id":1506249,"title":"","content":"Niggling terminology issue Exception Luck is an example spell, it can be cast as a Rote, Improvised Spell or a Praxis. <br /> <br /> I have to say my favourite Arcana at the moment is Death, mostly for the Absence purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T12:07:48-07:00","id":1506254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506231-let-s-talk-about-rotes-baby?p=1506249#post1506249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Niggling terminology issue</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone else seemed to get what I was asking and what I meant. Don't be *that* person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to say my favourite Arcana at the moment is Death, mostly for the Absence purview. </div> </div> </div>Arcana are not rotes by any stretch, and what is the absence purview, I can't find that in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 03-23-2023, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T12:11:47-07:00","id":1506255,"title":"","content":"<u>Correspondence, Know Nature, Analyze Life, Mental Scan, </u>etc- Knowing and Unveiling spells tend to have a ton of useful Reach effects, but often also need their Range, Casting Time, and/or Duration boosted. A Rote can get a ton of Paradox-free utility out of them.<br /> <br /> <u>One Mind Two Thoughts</u> - Makes it easier to cast on the fly, and the spell itself is good for stressful situations. <br /> <br /> <u>Emotional Urging</u> - Simple, but good for pavlovian conditioning. More Reach means better utility.<br /> <br /> <u>Incognito Presence</u> - Throw in a custom Key Reach, switch Potency to Primary, and you'll never need to turn it off. The Key just needs to be simple, like &quot;Anyone who I have directly spoken to in the last five minutes&quot;.<br /> <br /> <u>Telepathy/Ritual Focus</u> - Psychic walkie-talkies!<br /> <br /> <u>Body Control</u> - Potency to Primary, Advanced Duration, and all of the Reach effects. Still over-Reach by 1, but that's at least an improvement. <br /> <br /> <u>Control Weathe</u>r - the spell's actual area-of-effect is a little hinky, but I've generally assumed that it enforces the specified weather within [Scale], with the natural consequences of that weather extending beyond that range. That being said, more Reach for the Scale and Duration, and giving it the gradual shift effect to keep it unDissonanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T12:38:47-07:00","id":1506257,"title":"","content":"Purview defines the general things the Arcanum encompasses.<br /> <br /> Fate has fortune and oaths in its purview (page 134), but its easy to forget it also has intentions. So you could make an Unveiling spell to know people's immediate intent (Convince you of something, seal the deal with X terms, keep Y distracted), as well as Aspirations and Obsessions if you focus on them, which are goals they intend to pursue.<br /> <br /> Time has prophecy, but it also has change (page 185). So you could make a Veiling spell that makes people think something was always like that and will always be. A prisoner didn't escape, this cell was always empty and will always be. There was never a rare tome here, this display case was and will always be vacant. You always had the Thunderbird's Shell, and it never left your desk drawer.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T12:46:41-07:00","id":1506258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506231-let-s-talk-about-rotes-baby?p=1506254#post1506254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone else seemed to get what I was asking and what I meant. Don't be *that* person.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Arcana are not rotes by any stretch, and what is the absence purview, I can't find that in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but you seem to be talking about example spells, not rotes.<br /> <br /> Absence of heat gives Death control over Cold. Absence of light gives death control over shadows/darkness, Absence of life gives Death control of ghosts and zombies.<br /> <br /> But Death has Absence itself in its Purview, it can just be seen as very broad, that and endings. You could use death to Fray the feeling of grief that you have for a missing/dead (absent) cabal mate.<br /> <br /> In the book check of 128 for the purviews of death.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T13:07:46-07:00","id":1506259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506231-let-s-talk-about-rotes-baby?p=1506258#post1506258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but you seem to be talking about example spells, not rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rotes are specifically spells with bonuses are they not? There's no such thing as a rote that's not a spell, right? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Absence of heat gives Death control over Cold. Absence of light gives death control over shadows/darkness, Absence of life gives Death control of ghosts and zombies.<br /> <br /> But Death has Absence itself in its Purview, </div> </div> </div>So if a mage wanted to create a vacuum, like the vacuum of space not like a shark vacuum, that would be death because a vacuum is the absence of matter? Or if you wanted to remove all sound, you could use death for that? That's interesting and somewhat counter intuitive, kind of awesome though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T13:52:19-07:00","id":1506260,"title":"","content":"I like to keep in mind with rotes a short story where there is a divination rote where the mudra was to make out with the subject. To remember that every rote contains the idiosyncrasies of the master that created it and that mudra actions don't have to be subtle or easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27690,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","user":"MorganG","date":". 03-23-2023, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T14:20:53-07:00","id":1506261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506231-let-s-talk-about-rotes-baby?p=1506259#post1506259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if a mage wanted to create a vacuum, like the vacuum of space not like a shark vacuum, that would be death because a vacuum is the absence of matter? Or if you wanted to remove all sound, you could use death for that? That's interesting and somewhat counter intuitive, kind of awesome though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use an Un(making/ravelling) of Matter to remove things, or maybe more likely Space... But there is more than on way to skin a cat.<br /> <br /> So whichever works.<br /> <br /> Also, any spell can be made into a rote by a master (see the attainment for making rotes). An example spell can be cast as an imporvised spell. Or if a character casts it often enough they can integrate it into their Gnosis becoming a praxis. Alternatively they can learn the rote from a master/grimoire and cast it as a rote spell.<br /> <br /> Three ways to cast example spells.<br /> <br /> The alternative to example spells is creative thaumatergy to create spells using practice and purview - these can also become improvised spells/rote spells/praxises in the same manner as the example spells listed in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T14:32:46-07:00","id":1506263,"title":"","content":"Death also gets Enervation (and Absence of energy) but Endings can potentially end spells (dispellation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T02:50:00-07:00","id":1506295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506231-let-s-talk-about-rotes-baby?p=1506260#post1506260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to keep in mind with rotes a short story where there is a divination rote where the mudra was to make out with the subject. To remember that every rote contains the idiosyncrasies of the master that created it and that mudra actions don't have to be subtle or easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since we kinda segued into it, what's everyone's favorite Rote idiosyncracy for a spell? Any spell. I'm partial to rousing oration for <u>Control Weather</u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T03:46:18-07:00","id":1506297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506231-let-s-talk-about-rotes-baby?p=1506295#post1506295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, since we kinda segued into it, what's everyone's favorite Rote idiosyncracy for a spell? Any spell. I'm partial to rousing oration for <u>Control Weather</u></div> </div> </div> </div>The social/political sciences equivalent of the Mad Scientist, using Politics in every Rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awaken